        "original_id": "daa22031-666f-50ee-8fb2-3315fd6fdbf4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: South American Youth Olympic Games\n- Organizations: Organización Deportiva Suramericana (ODESUR)\n- Places: Lima, Peru\n- Topics: Regional multi-sport events, city population\n\nFacts:\n- The South American Youth Olympic Games is a regional multi-sport event.\n- The Organización Deportiva Suramericana (ODESUR) organizes the South American Youth Olympic Games.\n- The first edition of the South American Youth Olympic Games was held in Lima, Peru, from 20 to 29 September 2013.\n- Lima is the capital and largest city of Peru.\n- Lima has a population of more than 10 million.\n- Lima is the most populous metropolitan area in Peru.\n- Lima is the third-largest city in the Americas by city proper population, behind São Paulo and Mexico City.",
